---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Machine from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Machine.astro";
import Loading from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Loading.astro";
import Code from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Code.astro";
import Stability from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/Stability.astro";
import ApiTable from "../../components/ApiTable.astro";
---
<Docs title="Probability machine" status="experimental" lede="A working Galton board. Each ball makes a fair coin flip at every peg, so the bins fill with a binomial distribution.">
  <h2>Default</h2>
  <figure class="ply-exhibit">
    <Machine interactive />
    <figcaption><b>Eight rows, thirty balls, fair coin.</b> Click or press Enter on it to run again with new random flips.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <Code lang="astro" code={`<Machine interactive />`} />

  <h2>More balls, a biased coin</h2>
  <figure class="ply-exhibit">
    <Machine rows={12} balls={120} p={0.3} interactive label="Probability machine with twelve rows and a coin that goes right three times in ten." />
    <figcaption><b>Twelve rows, 120 balls, p = 0.3.</b> The pile shifts left, toward 12 times 0.3, about 3.6 rights per ball.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <Code lang="astro" code={`<Machine rows={12} balls={120} p={0.3} interactive />`} />

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <ApiTable rows={[
    ["rows", "Rows of pegs, 2 to 16. There is one more bin than rows.", "8"],
    ["balls", "Balls dropped per run, up to 400", "30"],
    ["p", "Chance of bouncing right at each peg", "0.5"],
    ["interactive", "Click or Enter runs it again; the element becomes a button", "false"],
    ["autoplay", "visible runs it when it scrolls into view, paced to finish within five seconds; none draws the settled state", "visible"],
    ["label", "Accessible description. After each run the counts in each bin are added to it."],
  ]} head={["Attribute", "Effect", "Default"]} />
  <p>The element fires <code>ply-machine-done</code> with the final counts, so a demo can print them. Call <code>run()</code> to drop a new set, <code>run(false)</code> to sample a new set and show it settled, and <code>settle()</code> to jump to the end of the current run.</p>

  <h2>Without JavaScript</h2>
  <p>The server renders the pegs and a settled pile from the expected counts, so the figure is complete before any script runs, in RSS readers, and with scripts off. Reduced motion shows the settled pile as well.</p>
  <Code lang="html" code={`<ply-machine class="ply-machine" rows="8" balls="30" role="img"
  aria-label="Probability machine" style="--rows:8;--bins:9">
  <span class="ply-machine__funnel"></span>
  <span class="ply-machine__pegs"></span>
  <span class="ply-machine__bins">
    <span style="--n:0"></span><span style="--n:1"></span><span style="--n:3"></span>
    <span style="--n:7"></span><span style="--n:8"></span><span style="--n:7"></span>
    <span style="--n:3"></span><span style="--n:1"></span><span style="--n:0"></span>
  </span>
</ply-machine>
<script type="module" src="https://dario-loi.github.io/polytope/kit/js/machine.js"></script>`} />

  <h2>Loading indicator</h2>
  <p class="ply-cluster"><span style="--ply-loading-count: 4"><Loading /></span> <span>Two balls take turns falling through three rows of pegs. It inherits the font size.</span></p>
  <Code lang="html" code={`<span class="ply-loading" role="status" aria-label="Loading"><i></i></span>`} />
</Docs>
